    title = "The New Dialectic and Marx's Capital",
    year = "2002",
    note = {CORE ARGUMENT: Arthur defends a "new dialectic" reading of Capital in which the logic of the categories unfolds by a systematic dialectic modelled on Hegel's Logic, with capital as an inverted subject. (Based on the book's recorded thesis and reviews in search; the DOI found belonged to a review and is omitted.) RELEVANCE: Systematic-dialectic variant of the immanent reading: contradiction as internal to the categorial presentation, with the standards given by capital's own logic. POSITION: Systematic dialectic (Hegelian-Marxian).},
    keywords = "marx, systematic-dialectic, capital, High, INCOMPLETE, no-abstract"
